Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenXT]
Subject: [PATCH] blktap: cast ioctl argument for modern access_ok()

access_ok() takes a user pointer, not an unsigned long.

--- a/drivers/block/blktap/device.c
+++ b/drivers/block/blktap/device.c
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ static int blktap_device_ioctl(struct blo
 		return 0;
 
 	case SCSI_IOCTL_GET_IDLUN:
-		if (!access_ok(argument, sizeof(struct scsi_idlun)))
+		if (!access_ok((void __user *)argument, sizeof(struct scsi_idlun)))
 			return -EFAULT;
 
 		/* return 0 for now. */
